M11 conversation-gated objectives when a key conversation is playing.
M11_Mission_Controller_JDG advances only from Action_Complete(ENDED) of the
non-key conversations M11_Level_Intro_Conversation (objective 2 and the second
intro, which also starts floor-1 security acting),
M11_Level_Intro_Conversation02 (objective 1), M11_EVA_SydneyPinged_Conversation
(objective-2 HUD marker) and M11_EVA_Activate_Nuke_Conversation (objective 5
and its switch blip). M11_Start_Third_Objective_Zone_JDG adds objective 3 only
from the ENDED end of M11_Add_Third_Objective_Conversation.
ActiveConversationClass::Start_Conversation stops a non-key conversation with
INTERRUPTED at once when a key conversation is active (M11 has three). Retail
called Monitor_Conversation afterwards, so the stop was never seen and the
step was lost for good.

Register the monitor before Start_Conversation and accept INTERRUPTED and
UNABLE_TO_INIT for these ids. The stop starts a 1 s timer that runs the
original ENDED branch, moved unchanged into a Deliver_* helper. A timer, not a
synchronous call, keeps the INTERRUPTED callbacks that Release_Level sends
from acting on the outgoing world (the timer dies with the object). A failed
Create_Conversation (id < 0) takes the same timer. Each step runs once,
guarded by a saved flag on unused ids (controller 6-9, zone 3). The factory
value-initialises, so old saves load the flags as false. On the normal path
Start_Conversation never touches the monitor array, so the conversation, its
end and the objective timing are unchanged. The zone also zeroes its
conversation id in Created. Engine conversation code is unchanged.

